<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan to tender Thursday for up to 56,000T corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan to tender Thursday for up to 56,000T corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's MFIG corn-buying group said on Wednesday it will tender on Thursday for one 54,000-to-56,000-tonne shipment of U.S. corn.  </p>
<p>The MFIG group's main buyers are Taiwan's Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Industry.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>			 U.S. Gulf	  Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 54,000-56,000     May 16-30	  June 1-15</p>
<p>The group said it also has an option to buy Argentine corn with the same tonnage, with shipment slated for May 10-30 from an Argentine port.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
